ID: vr-58
Title: Occasional procedural blinking across supported heads

Status: DONE
Milestone: Post-M1 character liveliness
Dependencies: vr-20, vr-44, vr-45, vr-57

Purpose:
  Add occasional eyelid closure at rest and during speech across all five
  supported heads and their presentations without additional neural inference.

Tasks:
  Add one bounded randomized blink scheduler and shared eye-space deformation.
  Integrate Claire-family and native MPFB renderers and a live opt-out control.
  Preserve audio clocks, cursor tracking, selected-only resources and originals.
  Qualify open/closing/closed/reopened output and lifecycle in isolated fixtures.
  Update the source-backed book, guide, ledger and original issue/Project item.

Acceptance criteria:
  Both eyelids close and reopen, including wire/dot/grid optics, without
    changing speech data or deforming mouth/hair/other facial regions.
  Idle rendering sleeps between blinks; speech/gaze share their existing RAF.
  Hidden pages, disabled blinking and lost contexts cancel blink work.
  Reduced-motion preference defaults blinking off, with explicit user override.
  No new model, dependency, persistent speech data or automatic live-head reload.
  Retain numerical/rendered evidence and distinguish procedural cosmetics from
    anatomical accuracy, visual acceptance and universal performance guarantees.

Completion evidence:
  Shared blinking.mjs clock/lifecycle/GLSL; app.js and native mpfb.js/renderer
    integration, opt-out and initialized reduced-motion controls.
  Actual Claire/native appearance qualification04: all four human views and
    native wire/surface close/reopen with exact restored pixels and allocations.
    Open/closed/contact samples visually reviewed, not every frame/angle.
  Deterministic clock/lifecycle, native RAF/startup and 83 CPU tests pass.
    Player/manager/session DOM fixtures pass; native blink-sessions-02 qualifies
    all five real models, manager blink toggles, muted speech and owned cleanup.
    Keep sessions01's intermittent MPFB close timeout; vr-64 tracks its unknown
    cause. No universal frame-rate/shutdown or human-accuracy claim.
  Explicitly requested live owned-head replacement completed; preserved settings,
    current source and natural-blink=true read back. No sibling head restarted.

Completion log:
  2026-11-21 - Owner requests occasional blinks across all possible model/views.
    Existing live Claire/Hazel head stays loaded and is not automated/reloaded.
    Candidate browser fixtures own their server/profile/data and synthetic motion.
  2026-11-21 - Implemented and environment-qualified; late software frames may
    miss the brief closed hold, so endpoints and sampled cadence are distinct.
    Native initial-control publication now follows reduced-motion initialization.
    Owner separately authorized and received the live replacement.
